From f53e4857ee4db95b9c21030a570bb09149c1ff66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AdrianProk <Prokopczyk.Adrian@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:03:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] 3DS: Add a diagnostic mode to the standalone build
 (MAUSJAGD_PORT)

The diagnostic mode helps to analyze startup time and frame rate on
the emulator and on real hardware. It is on when diag.txt exists in
sdmc:/3ds/mausjagd/ or in the RomFS root. The file holds extra command
line options for the game start, e.g. debug channels; without options,
"--debuglevel=1 --debugflags=loading" is used.

In diagnostic mode:
- every log line carries the time since app start
- the backend logs when it is ready and the first frame after each
  change of the game resolution
- every 5 seconds, the backend logs frame rate, area converted for the
  GPU, and time spent converting and in the whole screen update

Without diag.txt, nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
